    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0395" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg323"/>

                <head>Inhabitants of Plaistow</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Plaistow</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-volume-rules" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1865-07-31T23:59:59+00:00" notBefore="1865-04-15T00:00:00+00:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">From the inhabitants of Plaistow, Essex, England, in
                        public meeting assembled</hi>.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To Mrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lincoln:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Madam</hi>: Many words in your present grief
                    would be an intrusion. “We have expressed in another form our sympathy with the
                    loss sustained by the United States as a nation. Here, and to you, we would only
                    say that, as men and women of kindred race to your own, and, therefore, of the
                    same Christian family, we fully share in the grief felt by those more
                    immediately near to you. Distance does not create division in a common sorrow;
                    may that sorrow felt most keenly by yourself be assuaged by the Great Healer,
                    and to his tender mercy we affectionately commit you and yours.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Signed on behalf of the meeting:</salute>
                    <signed>JOHN FOSTER, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
